15 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating the process of adverse event reporting for pembrolizumab and nivolumab, showing initial data sources, removal of duplicates, categorization of adverse events, subsequent analysis using Reporting Odds Ratio, Proportional Reporting Ratio, and Bayesian Confidence Propagation Neural Network, concluding with descriptive, signal, onset, and mortality risk analyses.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a world map colored to represent the number of clinical trials for pembrolizumab by country, while panel B displays the same data for nivolumab. Panel C is a line chart comparing the annual trend of trials for both drugs from 2014 to 2023. Panels D through H are grouped bar charts; panel D compares trial counts by gender, panel E by disease type, panel F by trial phase, panel G by sample size, and panel H by cancer type, with pembrolizumab and nivolumab represented in dark and light blue, respectively.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Two Venn diagrams labeled A and B compare three sets each: ROR, PRR, and BCPNN, with set names in blue. Diagram A shows numeric overlaps: ROR only has 3, PRR only 4, PRR-BCPNN overlap 0, ROR-BCPNN overlap 6, ROR-PRR overlap 46, all three overlap 33. Diagram B shows ROR only 1, PRR only 9, PRR-BCPNN overlap 0, ROR-BCPNN overlap 5, ROR-PRR overlap 59, all three overlap 53.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Side-by-side panels labeled A and B display tabular and forest plot data for adverse events. Both tables list System Organ Class \(SOC\), Preferred Term \(PT\), counts, and reporting odds ratios \(ROR\) with confidence intervals. Horizontal bar plots visualize RORs for each row, demonstrating relative frequencies and confidence intervals for specific adverse events. Panel B contains distinct events and RORs from those in panel A.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Side-by-side tables labeled A and B list medical conditions with columns for system organ class, preferred term, total cases, and ROR with 95 percent confidence intervals, accompanied by forest plots displaying the odds ratios for each condition.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Side-by-side data visualization compares immune-mediated adverse event profiles for pembrolizumab and nivolumab. Panel A shows horizontal bar graphs listing various immune-mediated disorders with corresponding reporting odds ratios \(ROR\) for each drug, highlighting notable differences such as higher hepatic disorder ROR for pembrolizumab and higher myositis and cholangitis RORs for nivolumab. Panel B displays a bubble chart of adverse event categories, where bubble color intensity represents ROR and size indicates report quantities, facilitating comparison of event prevalence and reporting trends between the two treatments.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Side-by-side medical illustration displays two human bodies with labeled categories of systemic disorders. Panel A shows neurological, cardiac, hepatobiliary, gastrointestinal, endocrine, respiratory, skin, and renal disorders with specific immune-mediated diseases. Panel B lists similar categories but different symptoms and disease variations, such as memory impairment, cholangitis, pancreatitis, pemphigoid, and tubulointerstitial nephritis. Both panels connect disorders to relevant organs using color-coded lines for clarity.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a cumulative event curve comparing nivolumab and pembrolizumab over time in days, with both curves plateauing quickly. Panel B presents a cumulative event curve over a shorter time period, distinguishing pembrolizumab and nivolumab with visible divergence. Panel C is a heatmap illustrating frequency of various disorder types over defined time intervals for one group, using a blue color gradient. Panel D displays a similar heatmap for another group, with each disorder type compared across multiple time intervals, and frequencies encoded by color intensity.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
